throat:
n. the passage to the stomach and lungs; in the front part of the neck below the chin and above the collarbone
n. an opening in the vamp of a shoe at the instep
n. a passage resembling a throat in shape or function;

to:
prep. The preposition to primarily indicates approach and arrival,
motion made in the direction of a place or thing and attaining it,
access; and also, motion or tendency without arrival; movement toward;

trapdoor:
n. A lifting or sliding door covering an opening in a roof
or floor.
n. A door in a level for regulating the ventilating current;
